                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "A cute and simple puzzle game. It is short, but it takes at least one hour to complete all the levels for the first time. The graphics and the environment are very nice, and the experimenter character looks good. Being locked in an elevator, the game feels like a typical VR escape room style. However, it is not a typical escape room game. The gameplay is not versatile, unlike the rest of the genre, meaning you don't have to solve ambiguous puzzles with unintroduced unknown mechanics. All the gameplay is about putting the block pieces together with matching colors. Being under time pressure is the only challenge. And, it has a twisting end with a life message at the end. So, it is more like for kids or anyone who loves puzzles that seem like intelligence assessment tests for monkeys. Handling objects sometimes feels a bit janky, yet it is not a game-breaker issue. Graphically, every part of the place and objects matches together very nicely with the same unique style, nothing hurting the eye. It is not fun enough for a game entirely consisting of one puzzle style, yet I never got bored. So, in my opinion, it is a good game.",
